---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { COMPANY, CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../../config/product";
import { u } from "../../lib/url";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — DC Sim"
  description="This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and has no forms. Downloads are static files. Email us and we use your address only to reply."
  path="legal/privacy/"
  crumbs={[{ name: "Privacy", path: "legal/privacy/" }]}
>
  <article class="container page prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="direct-answer">This website sets no cookies, runs no analytics or tracking scripts and has no forms. The template and example files are plain downloads that do not ask for your email.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served as static files by GitHub Pages. GitHub may log technical data such as IP addresses to operate and secure the service, under its own privacy statement. We do not receive or use those logs.</p>
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>If you write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, {COMPANY} uses your address and message only to reply and to follow up on what you asked for. Ask us to delete the correspondence at any time.</p>
    <h2>Files you send us</h2>
    <p>If you send a filled template for a walkthrough, we import it only to show you your room, and delete it on request. See <a href={u("security/")}>security and data</a> for how the product handles customer data.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
